*.vo
*.vos
*.vok
*.glob

# Census .vo cache: the committed + hash-guarded census .vo bundle
# (tools/census_cache.py).  Un-ignore ONLY the committed census .vo so a
# regenerated census (make census-verify) shows up in git status.  Every other
# *.vo stays ignored as a build artifact -- crucially the census dir's OWN base
# .vo (Run/Decide/Deferred_*/Proven_*/TNF_QH/RankSearch/RepWLSearch), which are
# NOT committed and would otherwise appear as untracked noise after a build; the
# committed .vo directly under theories/Census/ are exactly the Run_Split* units.
# All of theories/Census/Compute/*.vo are committed walk units.
!theories/Census/Run_Split*.vo
!theories/Census/Compute/*.vo
*.aux
.*.aux
Makefile.coq
Makefile.coq.conf
.lia.cache
.nia.cache
.Makefile.coq.d
.coq-native/
tools/census_ladder
tools/__pycache__/
census_probes/
*.v.split
tools/repwl_sweep_stream.tsv
*.clog
base_build.log
